      "description": "Watch Amed vs Erzurumspor highlights and goals from Süper Lig on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 16, 2026. The Süper Lig encounter between Amed and Erzurumspor promised high-stakes action as both sides looked to make their mark. The atmosphere was electric for this mid-August clash, with fans eager to see how the tactical battle would unfold on the pitch. A Cautious Opening Half On August 16, 2026 , the match kicked off with both teams displaying a high degree of tactical discipline. The first half was characterized by a dense midfield battle, where neither Amed nor Erzurumspor could find the necessary space to create clear-cut chances. Defenses remained on top throughout the opening 45 minutes, leading to a stalemate at the break as both managers headed to the dressing rooms looking for a way to unlock the opposition. The Dia Saba Show The deadlock was finally broken in the 53rd minute, sparking a frantic period of play. Lumbardh Dellova provided a perfectly timed pass to Dia Saba , who clinical finish put Amed into the lead. The momentum shifted heavily in favor of the home side, and they didn't have to wait long for a second. In the 62nd minute, Gift Orban turned provider, setting up Dia Saba for his second goal of the match, effectively putting the hosts in control with a 2-0 cushion. Substitutes Seal the Deal Seeking to consolidate their advantage, Amed introduced fresh legs in the 64th minute, bringing on Gökhan Gül and Samuel Ballet . The tactical switch paid dividends almost immediately. By the 70th minute, the two substitutes combined brilliantly, with Ballet delivering the assist for Gökhan Gül to fire home the third goal. Despite a late yellow card for Rayan Raveloson in stoppage time, the home side remained professional until the end. When the referee blew the final whistle at 90+4', the result reflected a dominant second-half display that left the visitors with no answers."
